{"game": "remnant-2", "language": "english", "appid": 1282100, "month": "2023-11", "window": 2, "start_date": 1699401600, "end_date": 1700092799, "month_true_total": 4397, "quota": 39, "returned": 39, "pulled_at": "2026-09-12 14:54:19 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "150196497", "author": {"steamid": "76561198026955085", "personaname": "Sabamika", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198026955085/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 27, "playtime_forever": 8380, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3626, "deck_playtime_at_review": 263, "last_played": 1783708206, "avatar": "56532cd2448795bc16bb516d6ab6612471c5daa2"}, "language": "english", "review": "First off I want to say I do enjoy Remnant 2. If you beat part 1, you won't have any real issues skill wise with it.\nA lot of the new weapons are actually pretty fun. Like the Royal Hunting Bow, some of the archetypes are interesting and at first I was kind of put off by the idea. But slowly accepted it. And the fact they didn't do like last time, where the true final area was in a DLC like Subject 2923 is an improvement. The BIGGEST problem I have is no longer being able to upgrade armors and accessories. Don't know whose idea was, but you're just wrong for doing it. I get the idea why, to get more people to play multiplayer. But when it comes to particular fast/difficult bosses, that's going to be a problem.\n\nAll that aside, the game is still poorly optimized close to a year after initial launch.\nWhen it runs properly, it runs rather well. Even on my old obsolete RX 580. It can manage a solid 60fps with no issues. \nFunny side note, game runs fine on Steam Deck, despite saying it's not deck verified or not able to have it's graphics configured properly to run on it.\n\nBut when the game decides to freak out, it does so spectacularly. Everything from Freeze crashes to not properly displaying attacks from corrupt/aberrant elites. While in the same play session, boss attacks and ranged enemy attacks display properly.\nCould I recommend this game in it's current state? Yes, but not at full price. \nGet it on a site like Humble Bundle when it appears on Humble Choice. \nYou'd still need the DLC, but even after the complete version launches I'd suggest waiting on a sale. \nIF Gunfire ever gets off their buttocks and stops adding next to useless additions like boss rush and crossplay that I'm going to be honest, nobody actually wanted. And finally gets the game where it should have been at launch, only then could I recommend it at full price.\n\nSadly broken at launch/fix it after games seem to become the norm, when it shouldn't have. And if game devs want people to buy their products without hesitation, that needs to end.", "timestamp_created": 1700092591, "timestamp_updated": 1729470999, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "150196479", "author": {"steamid": "76561198232182512", "personaname": "Saulter", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198232182512/", "num_games_owned": 1614, "num_reviews": 23, "playtime_forever": 14920, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 14263, "deck_playtime_at_review": 455, "last_played": 1757198310, "avatar": "5076cb4b31180b9fb9b6520693e7906f4c89b8ba"}, "language": "english", "review": "Too many issues:\n\n1.Iv had constant stuttering since I got my new PC (4070) even with low graphics settings.\n\n2. They lied about steam deck support and had to be changed to unsupported.\n\n3. The game is about grinding the areas over and over (which is fine) but doesn't give you an actual reason to do this besides getting certain pieces of gear.\n\n4. Remnant FTA has continuous progression which made it fun to play even after 60+ hours, this game caps you at progression pretty early.\n\nTLDR: They made this game for 2 types of people:\n\n1. People who enjoy reading the code and making guides\n2. People who enjoy reading the guide and making themselves think they are smart for \"figuring out\" this \"puzzle shooter\"", "timestamp_created": 1700092557, "timestamp_updated": 1752532119, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150196311", "author": {"steamid": "76561198836294815", "personaname": "Gargerter", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198836294815/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 5639, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4520, "last_played": 1702773475, "avatar": "8896fe2a855fbb58ff1950e505477baefe5744ca"}, "language": "english", "review": "Loved the first one and this one is even better!", "timestamp_created": 1700092261, "timestamp_updated": 1700092261, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150196266", "author": {"steamid": "76561199244911156", "personaname": "Hogan", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199244911156/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 20742, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5584, "last_played": 1784592559, "avatar": "8dc62